.TH ATERM 1 "2026-10-24" "aterm" "aterm Manual"
.SH NAME
aterm \- a transparent, introspecting terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aterm
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B aterm \-\-window
.RI [ WINDOW\-OPTIONS ]
.br
.B aterm \-\-headless
.RI [ WINDOW\-OPTIONS ]
.br
.B aterm ctl
.RB [ \-\-sock
.I PATH
|
.B \-\-pid
.I PID
|
.B \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECS ]
.RI [ @<sel> ]
.I verb
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B aterm
.I verb
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B aterm
.I tool
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B aterm help
.RI [ topic ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aterm
is one binary. With a TTY it is the
.IR session :
it runs your
.B $SHELL
in a PTY and passes its bytes through unchanged; the host terminal draws them,
and the session keeps no screen and serves no control socket. With no TTY,
.B \-\-window
or
.B \-\-headless
it is the
.IR window :
a GPU terminal (Metal on macOS, OpenGL on Linux, Direct3D 11 on Windows,
with a CPU fallback) or,
headless, the same engine, PTYs and control socket with no window.
.B aterm ctl
reads and drives the window through that socket.
.PP
The binary also answers to other names, by
.IR argv[0] :
.BR aterm\-ctl ", " atpkg ", " agh ", " aterm\-fleet ", " aterm\-drive
and
.B aterm\-link
run those verbs,
.B amacs
is
.BR "aterm edit" ,
.B abrew
is atpkg's own stand\-in for Homebrew
.RB ( "aterm help abrew" ),
.B aterm\-gui
opens the window and
.B aterm\-cli
the session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-window
Open the GPU window (a launch with no TTY, such as from Finder, opens it too).
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Serve the engine and control socket with no window (announced on stderr).
.TP
.B \-\-session
Force the shell session (piped or CI runs).
.TP
.BI \-\-containment " MODE"
.B user
(the default: the launching shell's limits, no sandbox),
.B safety
(soft
.BR setrlimit (2)
caps of 8192 open files and, on Linux, 16 GiB of address space, which the
shell's rc can raise; Job Object limits on Windows) or
.B containment
(the macOS sandbox, with safety's caps as hard limits; refused off macOS).
Case\-insensitive; the last flag wins; an invalid value fails closed to
.BR containment .
.B \-\-sandbox
and
.B \-\-no\-sandbox
are shorthands for
.B containment
and
.BR user .
.IP
The sandbox allows no network or debugger attach, writes only to temp dirs and
shell history, and no credential stores or Mach services but user and group
queries, so
.BR open ,
.BR osascript ,
.B pbcopy
and the keychain do nothing
.RB ( "aterm explain\-config"
has the rest). A window brokers no OSC 52 clipboard, Kitty file or
shared\-memory image, or notification for a contained tab.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-reroute
Restore the upstream names (cargo, rustc, z3, ...) for this launch; see
.BR "aterm help reroute" .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Hide the session's startup line.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Session: on exit, print to stderr how many bytes passed through. Window:
routine startup notices.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " SHELL"
Print the bash, zsh or fish completion script and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
Print help or the version and exit.
.SS Window options
.B aterm \-\-window \-\-help
lists every flag and config key. A flag beats aterm.toml, which beats the
default.
.TP
.BI \-e ", " \-\-command " cmd [args...]"
Run
.I cmd
instead of the shell; takes the rest of the command line.
.B \-\-hold
keeps the window open after it exits.
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-working\-directory " dir"
Start in
.IR dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-control\-sock " path"
Bind the control socket at
.IR path ;
.BR 0 ", " off
or
.B \-\-no\-control\-sock
disables it.
.TP
.BI \-\-columns " n" ", " \-\-lines " n"
Initial grid size (20 to 500 columns, 5 to 300 lines).
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-px " n" ", " \-\-font " name|path"
Font size (points on macOS, pixels elsewhere; 6 to 200) and font for this
launch.
.TP
.BR \-\-gpu ", " \-\-cpu
Force the renderer (the last one wins).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " f"
Force the render scale; headless, the DPI of an
.B image
capture.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell " name|path"
The interactive shell to spawn.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shell\-integration
Start shells without the shell\-integration marks.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Print a diagnostics report and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
Each prints and exits without starting a shell:
.BR show\-config ,
.BR explain\-config ,
.B doctor
(checks this machine and repairs what aterm lays;
.B \-\-read\-only
changes nothing;
.BR "aterm help doctor" ),
.BR list\-fonts ,
.BI show\-face " family" ,
.BR list\-themes ,
.B list\-kitty\-commands
and
.BR exceptions " [" \-\-all ]
(what needs a look later, and filed entries).
.SH VERBS
.B aterm \-\-help
gives each a line and
.BI "aterm help " verb
its page.
.TP
.B aterm ship \fIargs\fR
Cut and release a build (needs a source checkout).
.TP
.B aterm update \fR[\fIcmd\fR]
Report or check for an update
.RI ( status " | " check " | " identity ).
.TP
.B aterm agents \fR[\fIcmd\fR]
Keep the aterm primer in coding agents' context files.
.TP
.B aterm machines \fIcmd\fR
Configure and manage a lab of Macs from this one over SSH, with no MDM and no
Apple account
.RI ( init " | " scan " | " enroll " | " status " | " plan " | " apply " | " person " | " screen );
macOS only.
.TP
.B aterm harness \fIcmd\fR
Claude Code's spend, limits and accounts, the disk, the approval ledger;
.B upgrade
moves a live Claude Code onto a newer build.
.TP
.B aterm keeper \fIcmd\fR
The PTY keeper (macOS, on by default: each window of an installed aterm.app
starts it if none runs; off is
.BR "[keeper] enabled = false" ).
.TP
.B aterm acaffeine \fR[\fIcmd\fR]
The menu\-bar keep\-awake mug (macOS), which every ordinary aterm window and the
converge pass start unless you turned it off. A click keeps this Mac awake or lets
it sleep, a right click picks 1, 8 or 24 hours or forever, Enable at Startup, or
Quit; an off you choose lasts until you turn it on again. Commands:
.BR start ,
.BR on " [\fIspan\fR],"
.BR off ,
.BR status ,
.BR startup " [\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR],"
.BR quit ;
see
.BR "aterm help acaffeine" .
.TP
.BR "aterm new\-tab" ", " "aterm new\-window" ", " "aterm split\-pane"
Open a tab, window or split
.RB ( \-d
.IR dir ;
.B split\-pane
takes
.BR \-V " or " \-H ).
.TP
Fabric and fleet (Unix)
.B fabric
(mail between sessions and people),
.B link
(its bridge),
.B fleet
(membership:
.BR init ", " join ", " peers ", " allow ", " publish ", " sync ", " census ", " leave ).
.TP
Toolchain and agents
.B pkg
(the package manager;
.BI "aterm " tool
runs an installed tool from the managed store, never
.BR $PATH ),
.B agh
(GitHub reads) and
.B ai
(AI CLI logins and reviews).
.TP
This machine
.B init
(set up this macOS login) and
.B secrets
(the credentials vault).
.TP
Editing
.B edit
(amacs, aterm's editor),
.B theme
(colour themes).
.SH CONTROL SOCKET
A window serves a per\-user socket in a mode 0700 directory, speaking
newline\-delimited text, to same\-user peers that present the per\-launch token,
as
.B aterm ctl
does. Its verb table is generated from the engine:
.B aterm ctl \-\-help
(no instance needed),
.B aterm ctl help
or
.BR "aterm help introspection" .
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-sock ", " \-\-pid " or " \-\-host ,
a request naming
.BI @ sid
goes to the instance hosting that session, one from a shell inside an aterm
window to the instance hosting it
.RB ( $ATERM_PARENT_SESSION_ID ),
and any other to
.IR <dir>/aterm.sock ,
the newest instance.
.I <dir>
is
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/aterm
when that is set (Unix), else
.B ~/Library/Application Support/aterm
on macOS,
.B ${XDG_STATE_HOME:\-~/.local/state}/aterm/run
on other Unixes and
.B %TMP%\eaterm
on Windows.
.B \-\-host
drives another Mac's aterm over the fleet once that Mac allows it
.RB ( "aterm help workers" ).
.PP
A leading selector addresses a session of any same\-user instance:
.BI @s\- hex
(a session id from
.BR ls ),
.B @self
(your own),
.B @.\&
(the active tab),
.BI @ n
(a local number) or
.B @*
.RB ( subscribe
only). Verbs group as observe
.RB ( text ", " screen ", " cursor ", " search ", " blocks ),
capture
.RB ( image ", " cast ", " temporal ),
live
.RB ( subscribe ),
drive
.RB ( send ", " key ", " turn ", " resize ", " select ),
wait
.RB ( ready ", " await ", " wait ),
session log
.RB ( log ", " brief ", " mark ),
app
.RB ( spawn ", " close ", " tab ", " invoke ", " controls ", " settings ),
connections
.RB ( connect ", " disconnect ", " flows )
and discovery
.RB ( ls ", " instances ", " windows ", " mux ).
.PP
A terminal tab's tooltip and context menu add one
.B now:
line saying what its session log says the session is doing
.RB ( "now: running shell" ", " "now: approval \(pc bash" ", " "now: limit \(pc 14:05" );
while the tab needs you, that comes first, and a label another program set with
.B mark
never shows there.
For 30 seconds after the harness restarts or upgrades an agent, or types its carry-on
after a full disk or a usage limit, the line says so with its author
.RB ( "now: restarting \(pc by the harness" ).
The tab's name is unchanged.
.B "[session_log] clause = false"
turns the line off, and the tooltip and menu are then as before.
.PP
.B aterm ctl
exits:
.TP
.B 0
the server answered
.BR OK ;
for
.BR ls / instances / windows ,
at least one instance answered.
.TP
.B 1
an
.B ERR
reply, or a usage or connection error; for
.BR ls / instances / windows ,
a socket directory holding no instance.
.TP
.B 2
could not reach: the instance accepted the connection but did not serve it
within 10 seconds; for
.BR ls / instances / windows ,
no socket answered, or the directory is missing or unreadable.
.TP
.B 75
a
.BR subscribe ,
blocking read,
.B turn
or
.B post
whose instance went away mid\-exchange, with nothing replacing it.
.TP
.B 124
a timeout: the client's
.B \-\-timeout
or one the server reported.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell a session or new tab runs (Unix).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Locates aterm.toml (FILES).
.TP
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Locate the control socket directory (CONTROL SOCKET) and, on Linux, the logs.
.PP
No environment variable sets the containment mode. A shell an aterm window or
headless instance spawns gets
.BR TERM=xterm\-256color ", " COLORTERM=truecolor ", " TERM_PROGRAM=aterm ,
.BR TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION ", " ATERM_CHILD=1 ", " ATERM_SESSION_ID ,
.B ATERM_PARENT_SESSION_ID
(its session's id, which
.B @self
names) and the tool directory on
.BR PATH ;
a plain session's shell gets only the tool directory. Every spawned shell
starts without AI\-tool variables
.RB ( CLAUDE* ", " ANTHROPIC_* ", " COPILOT_* ", " CODEX_* ", " ANTIGRAVITY_* ", " GEMINI_* ", " CURSOR_* ", " GROK_* ", " XAI_* ", " KIMI_* ", " MOONSHOT_* ", " AI_* ", " _DEVTOOL_* ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <config>/aterm/aterm.toml
The configuration; the window reloads its live settings on save.
.I <config>
is
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set, else
.B %APPDATA%
on Windows, else
.BR ~/.config ;
.B aterm explain\-config
shows the path.
.TP
.IR <dir>/aterm\-<pid>.sock ", " <dir>/aterm\-<pid>.token
An instance's control socket and per\-launch token;
.I <dir>/aterm.sock
links to the newest.
.TP
.IR <logs>/aterm.log ", " <logs>/messages.log
The detailed log, and every message aterm showed or recorded; each rotates,
keeping one older copy.
.I messages.wire.log
holds what scripts posted.
.I <logs>
is
.B ~/Library/Logs/aterm
(macOS),
.B ${XDG_STATE_HOME:\-~/.local/state}/aterm/logs
(Linux) or
.B %LOCALAPPDATA%\eaterm\elogs
(Windows).
.TP
.I <logs>/session\-log/
A window's session journal (macOS and Linux, while
.B restore_session
is on;
.B "[session_log] journal = false"
turns it off): each session's log as
.IB <instance> . <n> .slog
segments, 0600 in a 0700 folder, the oldest deleted first to keep it near
64 MiB and 2048 files (files a running instance is still writing can hold it
above that), so
.B aterm ctl @<sid> log
and
.B aterm ctl @<sid> brief
answer for a session from an earlier run. It keeps each command's program name
once a program of that name ran (the wrapper's own name when the wrapper's
flags are not known) or a shell builtin's name and, for a listed tool, one
known subcommand word, the session's folder, its meta values (an attention
text only as a fingerprint) and mail's senders and recipients; never a word
that ran nothing (such as a secret typed at a prompt), a command's other
arguments, an OSC title, a mail's body or an agent's transcript text. Off,
nothing is created there, and nothing already there is deleted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
aterm                                  # an interactive shell
aterm \-\-sandbox                        # the same shell under the macOS sandbox
aterm \-\-headless \-\-control\-sock /tmp/a.sock \-\-columns 110 \-\-lines 32 &
aterm ctl \-\-sock /tmp/a.sock image /tmp/before.png
aterm ctl ls                           # every session of every instance
aterm ctl @self text                   # this tab's screen
.fi
